## Limitations

- Exchange adds `SMTP` to a certificate on its own, for example when it is enabled for IMAP or POP. The resource only reads the services listed in `services`, so this shows no difference; an imported resource lists them all.
- Mailbox servers only.

{{ .SchemaMarkdown | trimspace }}

## Permissions

The provider's account needs `Get-ExchangeCertificate` and `Enable-ExchangeCertificate`, from the **Exchange Server Certificates** management role. The role group created by [`tools/new_role_group.ps1`](https://github.com/workplace-as-code/terraform-provider-msexchangeserver/blob/main/tools/new_role_group.ps1) grants them through a custom role without `Export-ExchangeCertificate`, which exports private keys. See the [Authentication guide](https://registry.terraform.io/providers/workplace-as-code/msexchangeserver/latest/docs/guides/authentication).

## Microsoft documentation

- [`Enable-ExchangeCertificate`](https://learn.microsoft.com/powershell/module/exchangepowershell/enable-exchangecertificate?view=exchange-ps)
